.TH GGE\-MENU 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-menu \- selectable lists for titles, pauses, options and shops
.SH DESCRIPTION
A \fBMenu\fR (menu.h) is a vertical list of up to MENU_MAX_ITEMS (12) text items. It handles keyboard (arrows or W/S, Enter or space), gamepad (dpad, PAD_SOUTH) and mouse (hover selects, click activates) and draws itself with a font you choose. Each item is a label and an action function taking the Engine. It is presentation state: one static per scene, rebuilt in on_enter.
.PP
.SH A TITLE SCREEN
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include "menu.h"
static Menu menu;
static Font font;
\&
static void play(Engine *e)     { game_state_init(e\->user); engine_replace(e, game_scene()); }
static void cont(Engine *e)     { if (save_load(&e\->save, "slot1", e\->user, sizeof(GameState), SAVE_VERSION)) engine_replace(e, game_scene()); }
static void options(Engine *e)  { engine_push(e, options_scene()); }
static void quit(Engine *e)     { engine_quit(e); }
\&
static void on_enter(Engine *e, Scene *s) {
  (void)s;
  font = text_load_font("fonts/ui.ttf", 12);
  menu_init(&menu, 0, 0, font);
  menu_add(&menu, "New game", play);
  if (save_exists(&e\->save, "slot1")) menu_add(&menu, "Continue", cont);
  menu_add(&menu, "Options", options);
  menu_add(&menu, "Quit", quit);
  menu_center(&menu, e);
  menu.y += 30;                          /* leave room for the title above */
}
static void handle_input(Engine *e, Scene *s, const Input *in) { (void)s; menu_handle_input(&menu, e, in); }
static void render(Engine *e, Scene *s, float alpha) {
  (void)s; (void)alpha;
  int w, h; text_size(font, "CATS", &w, &h);
  text_draw(font, (e\->logical_w \- w) / 2.0f, 40, COLOR_WHITE, "CATS");
  menu_render(&menu);
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Labels must outlive the menu: literals or static buffers, never locals. Actions run inside menu_handle_input, so a scene change they request takes effect after handle_input returns, like any other push or pop.
.PP
.SH THE CALLS
.TP
\fBmenu_init(m, x, y, font)\fR
reset: no items, position, font (a zero Font is the debug font), default colors and spacing.
.TP
\fBmenu_add(m, label, action)\fR
append; action may be NULL for a heading or a disabled line.
.TP
\fBmenu_center(m, e)\fR
center the block on the logical screen from its widest label and item count.
.TP
\fBmenu_handle_input(m, e, in)\fR
navigation and activation; from handle_input.
.TP
\fBmenu_render(m)\fR
draw; from render, after the backdrop.
Fields you may set after menu_init: \fBx\fR, \fBy\fR (position), \fBline_h\fR (spacing), \fBhit_w\fR (click width), \fBcolor\fR and \fBcolor_selected\fR, and \fBselected\fR to preselect an item.
.PP
.SH DYNAMIC LABELS
For values that change (volume, difficulty, a key binding), point the label at a static buffer and rewrite it in the action:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
static char diff_label[32];
static const char *names[] = { "Easy", "Normal", "Hard" };
static void cycle_difficulty(Engine *e) {
  GameState *g = e\->user;
  g\->difficulty = (g\->difficulty + 1) % 3;
  snprintf(diff_label, sizeof diff_label, "Difficulty: %s", names[g\->difficulty]);
}
/* on_enter: fill it once, then */ menu_add(&menu, diff_label, cycle_difficulty);
.EE
.RE
.PP
Left/right adjustment is not built in; either cycle on activate as above, or read \fBkey_pressed(in, KEY_LEFT/RIGHT)\fR in the scene's handle_input, check \fBmenu.selected\fR, and adjust the matching value.
.PP
.SH MENUS THAT DEPEND ON STATE
A shop, a level select or an inventory list is rebuilt from GameState each time the scene is entered (menu_init clears it). The action needs to know which item was chosen: read \fBmenu.selected\fR inside a shared action, or keep a parallel array mapping item index to item id:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
static int shop_ids[MENU_MAX_ITEMS];
static void rebuild(Engine *e);
static void buy(Engine *e) { GameState *g = e\->user; try_buy(g, shop_ids[menu.selected]); rebuild(e); }
static void rebuild(Engine *e) {
  GameState *g = e\->user;
  menu_init(&menu, 20, 20, font);
  for (int i = 0; i < g\->shop_count && menu.count < MENU_MAX_ITEMS \- 1; ++i) {
    shop_ids[menu.count] = g\->shop[i].id;
    menu_add(&menu, item_label(g\->shop[i].id), buy);   /* item_label returns a static or table string */
  }
  menu_add(&menu, "Leave", leave);
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rebuilding resets \fBselected\fR to 0; save and restore it around the rebuild if the cursor should stay put. More than 12 entries: paginate (Next/Previous items) or build your own list with text_draw and a selection index; the menu module is for short lists.
.PP
.SH BACKDROPS AND DECORATION
The menu draws only its labels. Draw a panel first: \fBdraw_rect(rect(menu.x \- 16, menu.y \- 8, menu.hit_w + 32, menu.count * menu.line_h + 16), rgba(0, 0, 0, 200))\fR. A pause menu dims the whole game with a translucent full\-screen rectangle. A cursor sprite goes at \fB(menu.x \- 12, menu.y + menu.selected * menu.line_h)\fR.
.PP
.SH CONFIRMATIONS
A two\-item menu in its own overlay scene ("Quit without saving?" Yes / No) is the standard confirm dialog. Pass the pending decision through an opener that stores a function pointer in a static; Yes calls it and pops, No pops.
.PP
.SH MOUSE BEHAVIOR
While the pointer rests over an item that item stays selected, which overrides keyboard movement until the mouse leaves the list. Games that are keyboard\-first can leave the mouse parked outside the menu block; otherwise it feels natural.
.PP
.SH PITFALLS
.IP \(bu 2
A label that is a local array: it dangles after on_enter returns. Use a static.
.IP \(bu 2
Calling menu_init in render: the menu resets every frame.
.IP \(bu 2
More than 12 items: silently dropped.
.IP \(bu 2
Forgetting the ESC handling: menus do not pop themselves; the scene's handle_input decides what ESC does.
.IP \(bu 2
Two menus in one scene: possible (two statics), but only one should receive input at a time.
